Trove — native file manager for Unraid
======================================

A storage-aware file manager for the Unraid WebGUI: shares-first browsing,
an optional dual-pane workflow, and server-side background jobs with
staging → verify → atomic commit semantics.

Safety model (short version):
- All operations are addressed by typed roots (share / disk / pool) plus a
  root-relative path; absolute client paths are never executed.
- Mixing logical shares (/mnt/user) with physical disks/pools in one
  operation is refused — they can be two views of the same data.
- Copies stage to a temporary file, fsync, verify, then commit atomically;
  a move deletes its source only after verification.
- appdata / domains / system / isos are write-protected by default.

Configuration: Settings → Trove (job data directory, parallel jobs,
protection mode, expert mode). Until a job data directory is configured the
plugin runs read-only.

Project: https://github.com/turlamai/trove
